OL,3,GNEWSAMum retires from cafe set up in
OL,4,Ason's memory
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe founder of a community cafe that
OL,7,Fprovides mental health counselling is
OL,8,Fstepping down after 11 years at the
OL,9,Fhelm.
OL,11,FJohnny's Happy Place in Kettering,
OL,12,FNorthamptonshire, was set up in 2014 by
OL,13,Fthe family of Johnny Mackay, who died
OL,14,Faged 29 after years of drug and alcohol
OL,15,Faddiction and undiagnosed mental health
OL,16,Fissues.
OL,18,FHis mother, Denise Mackay, 78, said she
OL,19,Fhad decided to retire for health
OL,20,Freasons, but the cafe, on Rockingham
OL,21,FRoad, would go on.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,367,360,200,160,0,100
